{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"agent_message","text":"Under **SEC Rule 22c-1(b)**, the ETF’s **board of directors or trustees sets the specific time or times** for calculating NAV. NAV must be calculated **at least once daily, Monday through Friday**, subject to the rule’s limited exceptions. More frequent calculations are permitted; exchange trading does not require continuous NAV calculation.\n\n**Worth knowing:** **4 p.m. Eastern is customary, not a universally mandated regulatory time.** Most U.S. ETFs align NAV valuation with the close of regular NYSE trading, ordinarily 4 p.m. ET. The fund’s disclosed valuation policy governs whether an early exchange close changes its NAV time. NAV valuation time is also distinct from creation/redemption order deadlines.\n\n[Source: 17 CFR § 270.22c-1(b)](https://www.law.cornell.edu/cfr/text/17/270.22c-1)"}}
